# Never commit ROMs or romsets (METHODOLOGY 5.6).
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Written as `pleiads/`
# the pattern matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which quietly
# swallowed pkg/pocket/Assets/pleiads/ -- the folder the Pocket looks in for
# the ROM. git drops empty directories, so the package lost the one file
# telling users where their ROM goes, and CI failed on every push until the
# packaging backstop said so out loud.
/*.rom
/*.zip
/pleiads/
/phoenix/
/*.bin

# The verification corpus is tracked: the frozen machine states and MAME's
# snapshot of each, which are what the regressions are held to and what makes
# them reproducible from a clean checkout. Everything derived from them --
# reference renders, RTL renders, diff images, the report page, audio captures
# -- is regenerated by tools/regress_ref.sh, sim/run_video.sh and
# tools/make_report.py, so none of it is committed.
#
# This is also where the unanchored patterns above did their worst damage:
# artifacts/pleiads/ and artifacts/phoenix/ were both ignored, so CI's video
# regression had nothing to run against and skipped in silence.
artifacts/*/ref_*.png
artifacts/*/rtl_*.png
artifacts/*/diff_*.png
artifacts/*/rtldiff_*.png
artifacts/*/attract_*.png
artifacts/*/e2e/
artifacts/audio/
artifacts/index.html
artifacts/**/*.wav
artifacts/**/*.ppm
artifacts/**/*.raw
artifacts/**/*.mp4

# MAME scratch
snap/
mamecfg/
nvram/
cfg/

# Build output
obj_dir/
projects/output_files/
projects/db/
projects/incremental_db/
projects/*.qws
build/
release/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
